2. Points 1,3,9,12,16:
   - One `<h1>` per page confirmed by Playwright heading dump (`headings.js`):
     Dashboard → single H1 "Dashboard", 8×H2, 2×H3, no skipped levels;
     Insights → single H1 "Insights", 5×H2, 5×H3, no skipped levels.
     `main`/`nav`/`header`/`footer` landmarks each occur once on both pages.
     period-context.html contains no headings, so LT1 cannot have changed
     this structure — confirmed by grep.
   - `<summary>` is the only toggle, keyboard reachable, toggles on both
     Enter and Space (`keyboard.js`): Tab-reached the "Period details"
     summary on /dashboard in both themes; `openBefore=false`,
     `afterEnter=true`, then a second Enter+Space cycle re-confirmed toggling
     both keys. Same served by native `<details>/<summary>` semantics (no JS
     needed) — confirmed present with JS off via raw `curl` of /dashboard and
     /insights (no `<details open>` remnants, "Period details" and "Prior
     period:"/"evidence bounds" text present in the raw, unexecuted HTML).
   - Visible focus indicator ≥3:1 both themes: screenshots
     (focus-light.png/focus-dark.png) show a rectangle around the summary in
     both themes. Pixel-sampled (PIL) the native double-ring browser focus
     outline: light theme uses a black ring (16,16,16) on white
     (255,255,255) = 19.0:1; dark theme's inner black ring is only ~1.3:1 on
     the dark card (31,41,55), but the SAME outline paints an adjacent white
     (255,255,255) ring at the identical position = 14.7:1 against the dark
     card — Chromium's native "auto" focus-ring renders both a light and a
     dark line specifically so one is always ≥3:1 regardless of background;
     this is unstyled browser default (no CSS in the diff touches outline),
     confirmed adequate in both themes.
   - Import CSV button and #drop-zone keyboard-operable with visible focus
     (`toolbar.js`): focusing `#import-csv-btn` then pressing Enter opened a
     real `filechooser` event in both themes; focusing `#drop-zone`
     (role=button, tabindex=0, ids/role/tabindex unchanged per diff) then
     Enter also opened a filechooser in both themes. `#import-csv-btn`'s
     focus-visible ring: light rgb(79,70,229) on white = 6.29:1, dark
     rgb(165,180,252) on the dark card (31,41,55) = 7.36:1 (computed,
     WCAG relative-luminance formula) — both ≥3:1.
   - No horizontal overflow at 390: see item 1 (0 overflow in all 8
