- Acceptance-3 in LT-RUN-SPEC.md ("multiset of trimmed text nodes ...
  identical except for added 'Period details'/removed 'Data freshness'")
  is, read literally at DOM-text-node granularity, not satisfied: master
  renders "Selected period: ..." and "Latest transaction: ..." as two
  separate `<p>` text nodes; the branch merges them into one `<p>` with a
  " · " separator per LT1.A.1's explicit instruction (which the task's own
  acceptance-2 Go test enforces). Every word/sentence is preserved
  verbatim and in the same order, fully exposed to assistive tech as one
  paragraph — no ACCESSIBILITY.md point or WCAG SC is violated by merging
  two adjacent one-line paragraphs into one. This is a tests-lane wording
  nuance (LT1's `checks` column includes `tests`), not an a11y defect;
  flagging for the lead/tests checker's awareness, not a FAIL from this
  checker.
- `web/static/css/tailwind.css` is a shared generated artifact rebuilt by
  `make css`, which scans ALL templates including LT5's concurrently-edited
  `insights.html`/`insights-investigation.html`. `make css-verify` passes
  against the current template tree, but this means LT1's checked-in
  tailwind.css may also carry classes introduced by LT5's in-flight work.
  Not attributable to LT1's own markup; noted per the concurrent-runs
  discipline in CLAUDE.md.
- One transient false alarm during this audit: an early screenshot
  (mobile-dark.png) appeared to show the Dashboard `<h1>` invisible against
  its own background in dark mode. Root cause: `<body>` carries
  `transition-colors duration-200`, and the screenshot was taken before the
  200ms CSS transition settled after `classList.add('dark')`. Re-tested
  with a 600ms settle (mobile-dark-settled.png): body bg rgb(17,24,39),
  h1 color rgb(243,244,246) — correct, high-contrast dark theme. Not a
  defect; recorded so the same artifact isn't mistaken for one downstream.

